I think the weight of the unicorn horn might be a sufficient factor for
monks who want to keep their encumbrance low. (Not me, necessarily; I'm a
pack rat whatever class I play.) Therefore, making it easier to cast
Restore Ability would make sense in that case. But the prospect of
*finding* a +oRA is much lower than that of finding a unicorn horn. Maybe
it should be added to the starting inventory rather than being given for
crowning.

I do like the HK movie effect of flying monks, but I don't kow that I'd
make that the monk's special spell. Giving *that* during crowning, though,
would make sense. 

> The ranger's special spell be changed to Identify, as Aragorn seemed 
> to always know the history and function of whatever treasure the hobbits 
> found.  Plus rangers need all the help they can get in this game.

As does everyone else. Rangers casting invis get to do so in combination
with a cloak of displacement or elven cloak, making for a very nice
combination. If they find a ring, they need not cast it again, of course
(but neither need anyone else). If the ranger's spell were to change, I
think cause fear or create familiar would be more in keeping with the
character.

